  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing Disease Prevention and Response to COVID-19 in Ejdabia, East of Libya</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed project will contribute to IOM&#x2019;s COVID-19 response in Libya, in alignment with the IOM Strategic Response and Recovery Plan COVID-19 for 2021 and WHO&#x2019;s Strategic Preparedness and Response Plan. The project will focus on supporting Ejdabia municipality in the East of Libya &#x2013; location which is particularly underserved. The overall objective of this project is to contribute to strengthening disease prevention and response capacity to COVID-19 in Ejdabia. To achieve this, IOM proposes a multifaceted approach that includes measures related to 1) Risk Communication and Community Engagement (RCCE) and promoting individual behavioural change related to prevention of transmission, and 2) improving accessibility to health and WASH services to support the community members to stay healthy. The project includes the provision of primary health care services, including screening for symptoms of COVID-19 in the community, accompanied by RCCE campaigns, and technical and material support to the local health facilities in order to strengthen their capacity for testing and treatment.</narrative>
  </description>
